# ThemisDB Error-Handling Audit – Ignore List
#
# Each non-blank, non-comment line is a path prefix (relative to the repo
# root) that will be skipped by tools/error_handling_audit.py.
#
# Rules:
#  - Lines beginning with # are comments.
#  - Paths are matched as prefixes, so "llama.cpp" also excludes
#    "llama.cpp/examples/foo.cpp".
#  - A trailing * acts as a wildcard for the suffix of that path segment.
#
# Add entries with a brief justification comment.

# ── Third-party submodules / vendored code ───────────────────────────────────
llama.cpp
vcpkg
ports
ports-overlays
ffmpeg

# ── Generated / build artefacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────
build
_build
out
dist
artifacts
releases

# ── Test infrastructure (may use nullable patterns intentionally) ─────────────
# Remove specific test subdirs from here once they are migrated.
tests

# ── Tooling scripts that are not production C++ ──────────────────────────────
# (Python scripts in tools/ are still scanned for PY rules)

# ── Archive / historical files ───────────────────────────────────────────────
archive
tmp_*
